{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 44, "model_name": "stockmark/stockmark-2-100b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a captivating film that delves into the origins and rise of facebook, one of the most influential companies in the modern era. directed by david fincher and released in 2010, the movie is based on the real-life story of mark zuckerberg, played by jesse Eisenberg, and his involvement in creating the social media platform.\n\nthe storyline is presented through a series of flashbacks and legal depositions, as zuckerberg and others are sued by former harvard classmates who claim they were the original creators of facebook. this narrative structure provides a compelling and engaging flow to the film, keeping the audience interested and invested throughout.\n\njesse Eisenberg's portrayal of mark zuckerberg is nothing short of exceptional. he captures the complex character with remarkable depth, portraying zuckerberg as a socially awkward yet brilliant individual. Eisenberg's performance is both convincing and relatable, making it easy for the audience to empathize with the character and understand the motivations behind his actions.\n\nthe supporting cast is also top-notch, with andrew garfield delivering a compelling performance as Eduardo saverin, zuckerberg's best friend and initial business partner. their on-screen chemistry is a highlight of the film, and the tension that develops between them as the story progresses is both heart-wrenching and compelling.\n\nthe film's direction and cinematography are equally impressive. fincher's direction is sharp and precise, capturing the fast-paced, high-stakes environment of the tech world. the visuals are stunning, with the use of color and lighting effectively emphasizing the mood and tone of various scenes.\n\nthe social network is a thought-provoking film that not only tells the story of facebook's creation but also explores themes such as friendship, betrayal, and the price of success. it is a must-watch for anyone interested in the tech industry or simply a well-crafted, engaging movie. the social network stands out as a prime example of how a biographical film can be both informative and entertaining.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.15321435034275055}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.006735715549439192}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -0.0004858981992583722}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.09133578836917877}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.1684512197971344}, {"token": " captivating", "logprob": -1.0315073728561401}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.4947192668914795}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.07900398224592209}, {"token": " delves", "logprob": -0.38426655530929565}, {"token": " into", "logprob": -0.0404457189142704}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0009059377480298281}, {"token": " origins", "logprob": -1.66007399559021}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.6957379579544067}, {"token": " rise", "logprob": -1.42648446559906}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.00100740697234869}, {"token": " face", "logprob": -0.0044519598595798016}, {"token": "book", "logprob": -3.755022044060752e-05}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.5402960777282715}, {"token": " one", "logprob": -1.0692766904830933}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.00020168177434243262}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0007983834366314113}, {"token": " most", "logprob": -0.011615739203989506}, {"token": " influential", "logprob": -0.058491501957178116}, {"token": " companies", "logprob": -1.5600218772888184}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.049048032611608505}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.2369130253791809}, {"token": " modern", "logprob": -1.397284746170044}, {"token": " era", "logprob": -1.6531965732574463}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.2980996072292328}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -0.8637482523918152}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -0.002415122464299202}, {"token": " d", "logprob": -0.16248999536037445}, {"token": "avid", "logprob": -0.009678345173597336}, {"to